<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Navezgane Hospital Challenge — UI/Menu
	Author: Frilioth
	Version: 1.9.0

	v1.9.0: the two Increasing Infection labels use text_key instead of literal
	text, so they translate. A literal text= attribute is never localised.

	v1.8.1: the preset values panel is now SHRUNK by the same amount it was moved
	down, so it no longer runs off the bottom over the Sandbox Options button.

	v1.8.0: Increasing Infection moved from the Advanced tab to the BASIC tab,
	directly under the Preset combo, styled to match Group and Preset.

	v1.7.0: the Increasing Infection control is now a vanilla ComboBoxBool, so it
	matches the other rows and greys correctly. It was two SimpleButtons.

	v1.6.0: section moved to the true bottom of the tab, and the Increasing
	Infection description corrected - with it Off the virus is disabled entirely,
	not merely held steady. Zombie hits are gated on the same cvar.

	v1.5.0: the Increasing Infection row now sits under its own heading and an
	explanation, instead of trying to pass as a vanilla gameoption row.

	v1.4.0: Increasing Infection row RESTORED. It is now recorded in flags bit 2
	of the HC-1 completion code, so a run carries proof of the setting.

	v1.3.0: Increasing Infection row removed for the v1 release. See the note
	where it used to be.

	v1.2.1: promo boxes actually hidden now - the v1.2.0 attempt targeted the
	window, which does not honour "visible". See the note above them.

	v1.2.0: title screen now shows the Hospital logo in place of the 7DTD one
	(texture swap, not a removal); the two promo boxes top-right are hidden;
	the new game logo is smaller and moved right to clear Chunk Persistence.

	v1.1.0: the three hidden options are now hidden with visible="false"
	instead of <remove>. See the note above them - removing them threw
	KeyNotFoundException and made the New Game screen unopenable.

	v1.0.0 (3.2 PORT) — FULL REBUILD. Every xpath in v0.3.4 was dead.

	WHAT CHANGED IN 3.2, all verified against the real vanilla file:

	1. The New Game screen was split into TWO windows.
	     newGame                  - game mode, world type, world name (leftPanel)
	     newContinueGameSettings  - the options, now spread across FOUR tabs
	   The old single window "newContinueGame" no longer exists, and the flat
	   .../rect/rect/rect/rect/grid path with it. Options now live at
	     newContinueGameSettings/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/scrollview/grid

	2. Of the 17 options v0.3.4 hid, only THREE still exist as <gameoption>:
	     MaxChunkAge, BuildCreate (x3), CameraRestrictionMode
	   The other 14 moved into the Sandbox Options system, so they are already
	   absent from this screen and their <remove> ops are dropped rather than
	   retargeted. For the record, the 14: XPMultiplier, DayNightLength,
	   BlockDamagePlayer, BlockDamageAI, BlockDamageAIBM, LootAbundance,
	   DeathPenalty, DropOnDeath, DropOnQuit, QuestProgressionDailyLimit,
	   EnemySpawnMode, AirDropMarker, AirDropFrequency, BiomeProgression.
	   NOTE: DeathPenalty IS in vanilla's file but COMMENTED OUT, which is why a
	   plain text search suggests it survives. It does not.

	3. The Increasing Infection row's anchor, gameoption JarRefund, is gone
	   entirely (JarRefund is a Sandbox option now). It is re-anchored to
	   PersistentPlayerProfiles, which sits in the same tab and is NOT hidden by
	   this mod. Anchoring to any of the three hidden options would break as soon
	   as the <remove> ops ran, which is why the insert comes first.

	4. The Starting Weapon row is REMOVED, not retargeted. That feature was
	   dropped: every run now starts with the same fixed kit, given by
	   game_first_spawn in gameevents.xml v1.3.0.

	5. Window "mainMenuLogo" no longer exists. gameLogo now lives in two places,
	   the mainMenu window and the newsScreen window. Only the mainMenu one is
	   removed here, matching the original intent of clearing the title screen.

	6. The left panel path changed. The old
	     newContinueGame/rect[@name='leftPanel']/rect[@name='newContent']
	   is gone; the world controls now sit in the separate newGame window.
	   PLAYTEST: the hospital logo position below is carried over unchanged and
	   very likely needs nudging, because it was tuned against the old panel.

	   menuBackground/bgTexture is unchanged in 3.2 and still resolves.
-->
<configs>

	<!-- Hospital custom menu background -->
	<set xpath="/windows/window[@name='menuBackground']/texture[@name='bgTexture']/@texture">@modfolder:UIAtlases/ItemIconAtlas/background.jpg</set>

	<!-- Title screen logo: SWAP the texture rather than removing the element.
	     Keeps vanilla's element, anchor and depth, and avoids deleting something
	     the MainMenuButtons controller may hold a reference to.
	     The vanilla element uses keep_aspect_ratio="BasedOnHeight" with
	     aspect_ratio="0.608" and height="400", so the SIZE must not be set here -
	     that would fight the aspect logic and squash the image. Only the ratio
	     changes: the hospital logo is 541x463, so 541/463 = 1.168. -->
	<set xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenu']/texture[@name='gameLogo']/@texture">@modfolder:UIAtlases/ItemIconAtlas/hospitalLogo.png</set>
	<set xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenu']/texture[@name='gameLogo']/@aspect_ratio">1.168</set>

	<!-- Hide the two promo boxes top-right of the title screen.
	     TARGET THE CHILD RECTS, NOT THE WINDOW. v1.2.0 set visible="false" on the
	     mainMenuNews <window> and it had no effect: vanilla never uses "visible"
	     on a window element (its only two uses in this file are on a rect and a
	     captionedtextbox), and each promo box carries its OWN binding,
	       visible="{% news_count > 0 }"
	     which is what actually decides whether it draws. Overriding that binding
	     with a literal false on each rect is what hides them.
	     HIDDEN, NOT REMOVED: both rects carry controller="NewsWindow" and the
	     parent carries controller="MainMenuButtons", so deleting them risks the
	     same class of failure as removing the BuildCreate gameoption did. -->
	<setattribute xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenuNews']/rect[@name='game']" name="visible">false</setattribute>
	<setattribute xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenuNews']/rect[@name='featured']" name="visible">false</setattribute>


	<!-- ================================================================
	     INCREASING INFECTION  -  BASIC tab, directly under the Preset combo.
	     It lived on the Advanced tab until v1.8.0; nobody looks there, and this
	     is the one setting in the mod a player actually needs to see.

	     Laid out to match the Group and Preset controls immediately above it,
	     copied from vanilla's presetSelector: label at 0,-20 font 28 centred,
	     full-width combo at 0,-40 height 38 font 30, same border colour.

	     ComboBoxBool is what vanilla uses for on/off options, so the arrows, the
	     boxed value, the On/Off text (localization_prefix="xuiComboOnOff", vanilla's
	     own keys) and the disabled styling all come from the engine.

	     GEOMETRY, AND THE ARITHMETIC THAT MUST HOLD:
	       vanilla   sandboxPresetValues pos 0,-250 height 320  -> bottom edge -570
	       here      this block 120 high at -250
	                 sandboxPresetValues pos 0,-370 height 200  -> bottom edge -570
	     The BOTTOM EDGE must stay at -570. v1.8.0 pushed the panel down 130 but
	     left its height at 320, so its bottom went to -700, past the window and
	     straight over the Sandbox Options button. The panel contains a scrollview,
	     so losing height costs scrolling, not content.
	     If this block's height changes, BOTH the panel's pos AND its height must
	     change by the same amount, in opposite directions.
	     ================================================================ -->
	<insertafter xpath="/windows/window[@name='newContinueGameSettings']/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/rect[@name='presetSelector']">
		<rect name="hospitalIncreasingInfection" pos="190,-250" width="${parentinnerwidth-190}" height="120" controller="HospitalIncreasingInfection">
			<label depth="4" pos="0,-20" height="30" style="hover" text_key="hospitalIncreasingInfectionLabel" font_size="28" color="[white]" justify="center" pivot="left"/>
			<combobox name="ControlCombo" type="ComboBoxBool" localization_prefix="xuiComboOnOff" pos="0,-40" width="${parentinnerwidth}" height="38" font_size="30" value_wrap="false" border_color="64,64,64,255"/>
			<label name="lblHospitalHelp" depth="4" pos="0,-82" width="${parentinnerwidth}" height="38" font_size="18" color="150,155,165" justify="center" pivot="topleft" text_key="hospitalIncreasingInfectionHelp"/>
		</rect>
	</insertafter>

	<!-- Move the preset values panel down by the block height AND shrink it by
	     the same amount, so its bottom edge stays at -570 where vanilla put it. -->
	<set xpath="/windows/window[@name='newContinueGameSettings']/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/rect[@name='sandboxPresetValues']/@pos">0,-370</set>
	<set xpath="/windows/window[@name='newContinueGameSettings']/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/rect[@name='sandboxPresetValues']/@height">200</set>

	<!-- ================================================================
	     NEW GAME MENU — hide irrelevant options
	     Only the three that still exist. See note 2 in the header.

	     HIDDEN, NOT REMOVED. XUiC_NewContinueGameSettings keeps a name-keyed
	     dictionary "gameOptions" and looks entries up directly:
	       ApplyCreativeModeChangeAllowed does gameOptions["BuildCreate"]
	     A <remove> therefore threw KeyNotFoundException on OnOpen and made the
	     New Game and Continue screens unopenable. v1.0.0 shipped with that bug.
	     setattribute visible="false" keeps the element in the dictionary while
	     hiding the row, and "visible" is a valid gameoption attribute in vanilla
	     (ResetUnprotectedChunks uses visible="{%iscontinuegame}").
	     ================================================================ -->
	<setattribute xpath="/windows/window[@name='newContinueGameSettings']/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/scrollview/grid/gameoption[@name='MaxChunkAge']" name="visible">false</setattribute>
	<setattribute xpath="/windows/window[@name='newContinueGameSettings']/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/scrollview/grid/gameoption[@name='BuildCreate']" name="visible">false</setattribute>
	<setattribute xpath="/windows/window[@name='newContinueGameSettings']/rect[@name='tabs']/rect[@name='tabsContents']/rect/scrollview/grid/gameoption[@name='CameraRestrictionMode']" name="visible">false</setattribute>

	<!-- Hospital logo — displayed in the new game left panel.
	     v1.2.0: reduced from 400x342 and moved right, because at the old size and
	     position it overlapped the Chunk Persistence row. 280x240 keeps the source
	     image's 541x463 aspect ratio (280 / 1.168 = 240).
	     These coordinates are an estimate against the 3.2 panel and may still need
	     a nudge - adjust pos here, no rebuild needed. -->
	<append xpath="/windows/window[@name='newGame']/rect[@name='leftPanel']">
		<texture name="hospitalLogoImg" depth="5" pos="240,-360" size="280,240" material="Materials/Transparent Colored" texture="@modfolder:UIAtlases/ItemIconAtlas/hospitalLogo.png" />
	</append>

</configs>
